=== CLI guards (no DB touched anywhere) ===
--- node scripts/migrate-positions.cjs (no --uri)
H04 position migration (dry-run first, additive, reversible)

Usage:
  node scripts/migrate-positions.cjs --uri mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/<db> [--manifest-out <path>]
  node scripts/migrate-positions.cjs --uri <uri> --apply

Default is a dry run: reads BriefingConfig tickers and existing positions,
prints a reversible change manifest, and writes nothing.

--apply guardrails (live execution is operator-authorized only):
  1. Requires HORIZON_MIGRATION_ACKNOWLEDGE=I-AUTHORIZE-LIVE-MIGRATION
  2. Requires a loopback (127.0.0.1/localhost) target unless
     HORIZON_MIGRATION_ALLOW_REMOTE=1 is also set explicitly
  3. Creates legacy_unclassified positions only; never modifies existing
     documents, users, briefings or briefing configs
exit=2
--- node scripts/migrate-positions.cjs --apply --uri mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/x (no acknowledgement)
Refusing --apply: live migration requires HORIZON_MIGRATION_ACKNOWLEDGE=I-AUTHORIZE-LIVE-MIGRATION. Live execution is operator-authorized only.
exit=3
--- node scripts/migrate-positions.cjs --apply --uri mongodb://10.0.0.5:27017/x (with acknowledgement, remote refused)
Refusing --apply: target is not loopback. Set HORIZON_MIGRATION_ALLOW_REMOTE=1 only after operator authorization.
exit=3
require is inert (no side effects): true isLoopbackTarget 127.0.0.1: true isLoopbackTarget 10.0.0.5: false
--- require of all five modules under a fresh node process
all modules load cleanly
